,title,link,text,language,family
0,"Gokana, Rivers - Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gokana,_Rivers","Gokana is a Local Government Area in Rivers State, Nigeria. The Gokana language, of the Ogonoid group of the Cross-River branch of the large Niger-Congo language family, is the main spoken language.",Gokana,Niger-Congo
1,Gokana | Accent Network,https://accentnetwork.com/gokana/,"April 22, 2025. Niger-Congo.Gokana, a Cross River language spoken by around 200,000 in Rivers State, Nigeria. Market Insights. Content is largely oral, with storytelling and local gatherings. English and Nigerian Pidgin are common among youth.",Gokana,Niger-Congo
2,"Tone Language Type Change in Africa and Asia: !XŨ, Gokana, and MPI",https://www.jbe-platform.com/content/journals/10.1075/dia.9.2.05rat,"This paper discusses three tone languages which have undergone different degrees of tone language type change and, as a result, are genetically or areally atypical: !Xũ (Khoisan), Gokana (Niger-Congo), and Mpi (Tibeto-Burman).",Gokana,Niger-Congo
3,Gokana,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Gokana.htm,"Gokana has a vigesimal numeral system with special structures for 9. Like most languages in Nigeria, there is a word for 400 'bóó'. The Gokana has three tonesː á=high, à=low and mid tone unmarked.",Gokana,Niger-Congo
4,(PDF) A Phonological Analysis of Gokana Sound System and its...,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/399888760_A_Phonological_Analysis_of_Gokana_Sound_System_and_its_Implication_for_Second_Language_Acquisition,"Gokana is used to refer to the language spoken by the people in Gokana local government area of Rivers State, Nigeria. Studying the phonology of Gokana helps to provide the peculiar features of its sound system, together with its vowels and consonants.",Gokana,Niger-Congo
5,What Languages do People Speak in Nigeria?,https://worldpopulationreview.com/countries/nigeria/language,"It is from the Niger-Congo language family and has as many as 24 million native speakers, both within and outside of Nigeria. There are over 20 dialects of Igbo, but Umuahia and Owerri are considered to be the official dialects.",Gokana,Niger-Congo
